      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It sounds deeply frustrating, and I hear that this feels like a creative compromise, not a technical one. The risk of getting flagged is real, and that kind of friction can kill momentum faster than any blank page. Maybe treat this as a challenge to build a different kind of tension—one that lives in restraint, atmosphere, or the unspoken, rather than direct actions or themes. If it truly becomes unworkable, that might be the nudge to pitch a fresh, separate project that lives outside those brand walls.",
